      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-11T19:51:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, there\u0027s no inheriting of limits like there is for toggles. A few lines above, we either unpack the user\u0027s required limits, or GetDefaultLimits; in both cases, unless the user specifies maxImmediateSize in requiredLimits, we\u0027ll get the default of 64 here.\n\nI discussed this with Corentin, and we agreed that overriding the limit to 0 if the toggles are not enabled is a hack, and we need to do it in both places. Also, keep in mind that both of these will be removed once this feature is enabled in core.",
      "parentUuid": "f768190d_796f8cc2",
      "revId": "5d26acb97f7b206fb97068aad97f40ad4909e216",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
